# Sentence case everywhere

Write all website copy in sentence case unless Diana says otherwise. Capitalize only the first word and proper nouns.

This covers page titles, headings, nav links, buttons, labels, form fields, alt text, product names, and messages.

- Good: "Shop crochet", "Add to cart", "Your cart", "Elf hat", "Wine bottle holders"
- Bad: "Shop Crochet", "Add To Cart", "Your Cart", "Elf Hat", "Wine Bottle Holders"

Product names: `name` in `src/data/products.ts` and `title` in `src/data/pattern-requests.ts` follow this too.

## Yarn color names

Show yarn colors in lowercase, except proper nouns: "Color: off white", "Italian cream".

- Keep the supplier's spelling in the data (`src/data/charisma.json`, `src/data/bobbiny-premium-5mm.json`, `name` on yarns in `src/data/products.ts`). Stock sync matches on those names.
- Wherever a color name is shown, wrap it in `colorName()` from `src/lib/color-name.ts`. Add new proper nouns to its `PROPER_WORDS` list.
- In hand-written copy (like product descriptions), type colors in lowercase.

## Exceptions

- Brand and proper names keep their own spelling: "Diana's art", "Flagstaff", "Charisma", "Loops & Threads", "Bobbiny", "Venmo", "Mountainaire General Store".
- Anything Diana asks to style differently.
